.TH IPHONE-MIRROR-SCREEN 1 "2026" "iphone-mirror-bridge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iphone-mirror-screen \- start or stop the iPhone screen-mirroring receiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iphone-mirror-screen
[\fB\-\-start\fR|\fB\-\-stop\fR|\fB\-\-status\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts an AirPlay receiver (UxPlay) named "iPhone Mirror Bridge" for the
current desktop user. On the iPhone, open Control Center, tap Screen
Mirroring and choose it. Without arguments the command toggles: it starts the
receiver if stopped and stops it if running. The "iPhone Screen Mirroring"
application menu entry runs this command.
.PP
The iPhone and computer must be on the same network. The receiver uses
TCP ports 7000, 7001, 7100 and UDP ports 6000, 6001, 7011, plus mDNS
(UDP 5353); allow them if a firewall is enabled.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.cache/iphone-mirror-bridge/uxplay.log
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uxplay (1),
.BR iphone-mirror-bridge (1)
